---
title: AI Horde worker
description: Share your model with the AI Horde, a volunteer network. How to set up the built-in Horde worker in KoboldCpp and what the options do.
sidebar:
  order: 10
---

The [AI Horde](https://aihorde.net) is a volunteer network: people run models on their own computers and others use them over the internet. KoboldCpp has a built-in worker, so you can share your text model with the Horde while you run it.

The worker only takes Horde jobs while you are not using the model yourself: it waits until there has been no local request for 20 seconds.

## Set it up

You need an AI Horde API key. Register at [aihorde.net/register](https://aihorde.net/register) to get one.

{% steps %}

1. Load your text model as usual.
2. In the launcher, open the **Horde Worker** tab and tick **Configure for Horde**.
3. Enter your key in **API Key (If Embedded Worker):** and a name for your worker in **Horde Worker Name:**.
4. Click **Launch**.

{% /steps %}

On the command line:

```sh {% title="Terminal" frame="terminal" %}
koboldcpp --model mymodel.gguf --hordekey YOUR_KEY --hordeworkername my-worker
```

Both the key and the worker name are required. With only the key, KoboldCpp prints "Horde worker could not start. You need to specify a horde worker name with --hordeworkername".

With a Horde worker, KoboldCpp switches to quiet mode automatically.

<!-- SCREENSHOT: Horde Worker tab with Configure for Horde ticked -->

{% aside type="caution" %}
**Save Config** stores your Horde API key in plain text in the `.kcpps` file. Do not share that file. Templates (`.kcppt`) leave the key and worker name out.
{% /aside %}

## Options

| Launcher field | Flag | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| **Horde Model Name:** | `--hordemodelname` | The model name shown on the Horde. Empty means the file name. KoboldCpp adds `koboldcpp/` in front. |
| **Gen. Length:** | `--hordegenlen` | Most tokens your worker generates per Horde job. Default `1024`. |
| **Max Context:** | `--hordemaxctx` | Largest context your worker accepts from a Horde job. `0` means your context size; it cannot go higher. |
| **API Key (If Embedded Worker):** | `--hordekey` | Your AI Horde API key. |
| **Horde Worker Name:** | `--hordeworkername` | Your worker's name on the Horde. |

## Advanced

- These three settings are not Horde-only. **Horde Model Name:** also renames the model in `/api/v1/model` and `/v1/models`. **Gen. Length:** and **Max Context:** are also what `/api/v1/config/max_length` and `/api/v1/config/max_context_length` report to other apps.
- With `--parallelrequests N`, KoboldCpp starts N workers under the same name.
- After repeated errors, the worker pauses for growing periods, and stops after too many.
- If the worker fails with certificate (SSL) errors, `--nocertify` turns off certificate checks for all outgoing connections. This is insecure: whoever intercepts the connection can read your Horde API key. Use it only as a last resort.

